# Heavy simulation artifacts are never tracked here. Saved Population objects, genotype
# matrices and per-generation dumps live under /n/scratch/users/n/nur479/ (prunable, not
# backed up) and are written there by the generate stage -- see README.md. These rules are a
# backstop for anything that lands in the working tree by accident: a local test run, a
# notebook writing beside itself, or a convenience symlink into scratch.
#
# The notebooks, the scripts and theory.py ARE tracked. So is any small summary table a
# verify notebook writes out, which is why this ignores data formats rather than a data/ dir.

*.pkl
*.pkl.gz
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
*.parquet
*.feather
*.bed
*.bim
*.fam
*.pgen
*.pvar
*.psam

# a convenience symlink to this writeup's scratch area, if one is made
scratch

# notebook execution leftovers
.ipynb_checkpoints/
